{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-3052","published":"2026-07-19T11:11:56Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:21:20.291864022Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-14355"],"summary":"php security update","details":"PHP is an HTML-embedded scripting language. PHP attempts to make it easy for developers to write dynamically generated web pages. PHP also offers built-in database integration for several commercial and non-commercial database management systems, so writing a database-enabled webpage with PHP is fairly simple. The most common use of PHP coding is probably as a replacement for CGI scripts.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nIn PHP versions 8.2.* before 8.2.32, 8.3.* before 8.3.32, 8.4.* before 8.4.23, 8.5.* before 8.5.8, the AES-WRAP-PAD algorithm implementation in OpenSSL extension contains a buffer allocation flaw. The output buffer for the AES key-wrap-with-padding operation is sized from the plaintext length without accounting for RFC 5649 expansion. This may cause OpenSSL to write beyond allocated memory, corrupting heap metadata and triggering application abort.(CVE-2026-14355)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"php","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/php&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["php-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-bcmath-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-cli-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-common-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-dba-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-dbg-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-debuginfo-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-debugsource-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-devel-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-embedded-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-enchant-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-ffi-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-fpm-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-gd-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","php-gmp-8.0.30-14.oe2003sp4.aa